  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 203.29 Standard of Proof",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 203.29 Standard of Proof. Unless otherwise specified by law, the standard of proof shall be by a preponderance of the evidence. “Proof by preponderance of the evidence” means a demonstration by admissible evidence that a fact or legal conclusion is more probable than not to be true.\n\nSource. #7349, eff 8-22-00; ss by #8230-A, eff 12-17-04 (formerly Saf-C 203.28)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c200.html"
